  "id": "38bc9a76-f0ca-5053-acfb-7794ecb99b33",
  "slug": "pepper-parm-prime-rib-recipe-8757842",
  "name": "Pepper Parm Prime Rib",
  "recipe_type": "main",
  "brief_description": "This pepper Parm prime rib is rich, savory, and roasted to medium-rare perfection\u2014an elegant way to prepare this premium cut of beef.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Optional step: Use a sharp knife to cut down 1/8 inch through the tough membrane on top, every inch or so, to prevent the tough membrane from contracting and distorting the shape of the meat as it roasts."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Salt beef all over and transfer to a rack placed over a roasting pan. Refrigerate, uncovered, for 8 to 24 hours."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Remove from the refrigerator and allow to sit at room temperature for 2 hours before roasting."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 450 degrees F (230 degrees C). Stir butter, cheese, and black pepper together in a bowl. This mixture needs to be very soft to spread evenly over the meat."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Blot any moisture on the surface of beef with a paper towel. Apply a few teaspoons of butter mixture to bottom and sides of beef, then spread remaining mixture across the top. Apply more black pepper and Parmigiano Reggiano to the top if desired."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Pour beef broth and water into the bottom of the roasting pan."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Roast in the upper center of the preheated oven for 20 minutes. Reduce oven temperature to 325 degrees F (165 degrees C) and continue to roast until the internal temp in the center of the thickest part reaches 120 degrees F (49 degrees C) for medium rare. Roasting may take a total of about 1 1/2 hours, but always use an instant read thermometer or meat thermometer to determine doneness rather than using a timer, as time will vary greatly depending on the size of the roast."
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "text": "Remove from the oven, and tent loosely with foil. Let rest for 20 minutes, or until the internal temperature has risen to 130 degrees F (54 degrees C), which will give you a perfect rosy pink center."
    },
    {
      "position": 9,
      "text": "Meanwhile, pour pan juices into a saucepan and keep warm over low heat until needed. Season with salt and pepper to taste before using."
    },
    {
      "position": 10,
      "text": "Slice meat off the bones, and then slice down into 6 portions. Serve on heated plates with hot \u201cjus\u201d alongside."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 6,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 85,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 15,
